 (status sourceUrl refKind markdown)←FetchReadme(projectUrl version packageName);urls;i;u;c;q;resp;answered;maxSize;rawUrl;blobUrl;text
⍝ Fetches a package's README from GitHub. Returns one of:
⍝ * ('ok' sourceUrl refKind markdown) - found; `refKind` is 'tag' or 'branch'
⍝ * ('none' '' '' '')                 - GitHub answered and there is no README to be had
⍝ * ('error' '' '' '')                - GitHub could not be reached at all
⍝ The last two matter because only a settled answer is recorded (see `FetchAndStoreReadme`):
⍝ 'none' is a fact about the repository and stands, while 'error' says only that this
⍝ attempt failed, and writing it down as 'none' would bake a network hiccup into the
⍝ Registry for good.
⍝ The rows are walked in the order `GetReadmeUrls` returns them, so every spelling of the
⍝ release's own tag is tried before the default branch is considered at all: a package
⍝ whose repository carries the tag never ends up with the branch's README. `packageName` is
⍝ passed on for the test that decides whether the branch is offered at all; see there.
⍝ A failed connection ends the walk then and there rather than moving on to the next
⍝ spelling: what failed is the connection to GitHub, not that particular URL, so the rows
⍝ left cannot fare any better, and trying them all would multiply one outage by the number
⍝ of spellings - each one waiting for `ClientTimeout` before it gives up.
⍝ It leaves as 'error' whatever earlier rows answered, which is why it returns rather than
⍝ leaving the loop: the spellings not reached were not tried, so 'none' - "we looked and
⍝ there is none" - would be a claim this attempt has not earned. The package comes round
⍝ again instead; see `ReadmeIsDue`.
⍝ A 404 is a different matter and does move on: that is GitHub answering, and the next
⍝ spelling may well be the one that exists.
⍝ A failed connection is not logged: it is recorded against the package as 'error' instead,
⍝ where it belongs, and logging every timeout would bury the log during a GitHub outage.
 (status sourceUrl refKind markdown)←'error' '' '' ''
 answered←0
 maxSize←262144                                     ⍝ 256 KB; anything larger is not a README
 urls←GetReadmeUrls projectUrl version packageName
 :If 0=≢urls
     status←'none'                                  ⍝ Nowhere to look is not a network problem
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :For i :In ⍳≢urls                                  ⍝ Loop over the spellings, most likely first
     :Trap 345                                      ⍝ Rumba turns every failed connection into 345
         (rawUrl blobUrl)←urls[i;1 2]
         u←R.ParseURI rawUrl
         c←R.NewClient rawUrl
         c.CongaTimeout←3000                        ⍝ Milliseconds; raw.githubusercontent is a CDN
         c.ClientTimeout←10                         ⍝ Seconds, for the exchange as a whole
         q←R.NewRequest u.Resource
         resp←⊃c R.SendAndReceive q
     :Else
         :Return                                    ⍝ Signalled: timed out, closed, or no route
     :EndTrap
     answered←1
     :If 200=resp.StatusCode
     :AndIf 0<≢resp.Content
     :AndIf maxSize≥≢resp.Content
     ⍝ What arrives is bytes, not text; see `Utf8ToText` for why it has to be decoded here.
     :AndIf 0<≢text←Utf8ToText resp.Content
         (status sourceUrl refKind markdown)←'ok'blobUrl(3⊃urls[i;])text
         :Return
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
 :If answered
     status←'none'
 :EndIf
